/-! # Isomorphisms of complete local algebras from the closed fibre

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0CBX, final paragraph, using Tags 00ME and 031D
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-flat-fibre-isomorphism).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- A local map of complete Noetherian local algebras with flat target is an isomorphism
if its closed-fibre map is an isomorphism. The intermediate maximal-ideal, residue-field,
finiteness and chosen-generator assertions are included.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0CBX, final paragraph
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-flat-fibre-isomorphism).

Proof:
1. Apply `flat_mod_injective` [lem-weil-pbc-flat-mod-injective] with base `A`, source
   algebra `C`, finite source module `C`, flat target module `B`, and map `φ`.
   The closed-fibre isomorphism gives its injectivity hypothesis, so `φ` is injective.
2. Locality gives `mB ≤ cB ≤ n`. For `b ∈ n`, lift its class modulo `mB` through
   the closed-fibre map to `c ∈ C`. Then `φ c ∈ n`, so `c` is a nonunit and belongs
   to `c`. Thus `n = cB`. The same lifting proves surjectivity of the residue map;
   its kernel is zero because a local map reflects units.
3. Completeness of `B` [def-weil-pbc-adically-complete-ring] implies separation for
   `n`, hence for `c` acting on `B`, since `c^r B = n^r`.
4. Apply `Module.finite_and_span_eq_top_of_adicComplete`
   [lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-complete-ring] to the complete ring `C` and module `B`.
   Its residue quotient is generated by the image of `1`, so `B` is finite over `C`
   and the chosen-generator assertion says that `1` spans `B`.
5. Generation by `1` makes `φ` surjective. Together with Step 1 this gives its
   inverse as an `A`-algebra homomorphism, and hence the asserted algebra equivalence.
No flatness of `C` over `A` is needed. -/
theorem complete_flat_fibre_isomorphism
    {A : Type u} {C : Type v} {B : Type w}
    [CommRing A] [CommRing C] [CommRing B]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing C] [IsLocalRing B]
    [IsNoetherianRing C] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal C) C] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal B) B]
    [Algebra A C] [Algebra A B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A C)] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
    (φ : C →ₐ[A] B) [IsLocalHom φ.toRingHom] [Module.Flat A B]
    (hFibre : Function.Bijective
      ((maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A C)).mapQ
        (maximalIdeal A • (⊤ : Submodule A B)) φ.toLinearMap
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top (maximalIdeal A) φ.toLinearMap))) :
    Function.Injective φ ∧
      (maximalIdeal C).map φ.toRingHom = maximalIdeal B ∧
      Function.Bijective (ResidueField.map φ.toRingHom) ∧
      @Module.Finite C B _ _ (Module.compHom B φ.toRingHom) ∧
      @Submodule.span C B _ _ (Module.compHom B φ.toRingHom) {1} = ⊤ ∧
      ∃ e : C ≃ₐ[A] B, e.toAlgHom = φ := by
  sorry

end IsLocalRing
